  "ehiExportPage": {
    "wordCount": 287,
    "articleText": "Electronic Health Information Export This document offers insights into the format of the export output when utilizing the smartEMR Electronic Health Information (EHI) export feature. The primary objective is to ensure compliance with the 2015 Edition Cures Update Conformance Regulation §170.315(b)(10) for Electronic Health Information export. CDA Format (Clinical Document Architecture) Single patient electronic health information export: Each unique patient encounter is meticulously documented within a CDA file, adhering to the rigorous specifications and standards set by HL7 CDA. Admin Panel → Export Options → Patient Data → Create a backup/export By Patient Select patient(s), click on &quot;Create&quot; Additional Options include: Schedule a one-time backup/export Schedule a recurring backup/export Search by Date of Service Patient population electronic health information export: For a comprehensive overview, a consolidated CDA file is available, amalgamating all patient encounters pertaining to a specific individual. Admin Panel → Export Options → Patient Data → Create a backup/export All Patients Click on &quot;Select All&quot; patients, and click on &quot;Create&quot; Additional Options include: Schedule a one-time backup/export Schedule a recurring backup/export Search by Date of Service Document Repository (Scanned or Upload Documents in PDF, JPG, PNG Formats) This repository encompasses a range of signed encounter notes, lab results, radiology reports, and any other scanned or uploaded documents within a patient&#x27;s record. All documents are sorted and indexed within the respective patient chart ID number folders. In cases where specific categories or types of documents exist (e.g., Lab Reports, Radiology, Scanned Receipts, etc.), they are housed within dedicated category subfolders under the primary patient folder. Admin Panel →Export Options → Patient Document Data (b10) Search patient criteria, select a single patient or ALL, click on &quot;Create Portable&quot; Updated 11 months ago Patient Demographic (PM) Ask AI"
  }
}